<title>BELGIUM: SAIT 1996 group net profit rises 39 pct.</title>
<headline>SAIT 1996 group net profit rises 39 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit		   101.8  vs     73.4</p>
<p>    Cons pre-tax profit		 68.9  vs    135.7</p>
<p>    Cons turnover		   11,195.2  vs 10,704.3</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   307.0  vs    334.2</p>
<p>    Current pre-tax profit	    93.9  vs    134.3</p>
<p>    Financial loss		     213.1  vs    199.9</p>
<p>    Exceptional gains		   22.7  vs	1.4</p>
<p>    Gross dividend/share (francs)   21    vs     16</p>
<p>    Cash-flow			    505    vs    370</p>
<p>NOTE - SAIT-RadioHolland, a Belgo-Dutch telecommunications group, said in a statement that its operating profit slipped due to changes in the consolidation perimeter and depreciation on commercial debt claims within Strategic Business Unit (SBU) Communications, partly due to the bankruptcy of a major client.</p>
<p>-- Bert Lauwers, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
